{"id":4279,"date":"2020-02-17T14:39:23","date_gmt":"2020-02-17T20:39:23","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/pokernight.com\/55-2-2\/"},"modified":"2020-02-17T14:42:17","modified_gmt":"2020-02-17T20:42:17","slug":"55-2-2","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/pokernight.com\/55-2-2\/","title":{"rendered":"HIGH STAKES CASH GAMES RETURN TONIGHT 10pmET"},"content":{"rendered":"<p>[et_pb_section fb_built=&#8221;1&#8243; _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.5&#8243; use_background_color_gradient=&#8221;on&#8221; background_color_gradient_start=&#8221;#f2f2f2&#8243; background_color_gradient_end=&#8221;#f2f2f2&#8243; custom_padding=&#8221;0px|||||&#8221;][et_pb_row _builder_version=&#8221;3.25&#8243;][et_pb_column type=&#8221;4_4&#8243; _builder_version=&#8221;3.25&#8243; custom_padding=&#8221;|||&#8221; custom_padding__hover=&#8221;|||&#8221;][et_pb_text _builder_version=&#8221;4.3.2&#8243; background_size=&#8221;initial&#8221; background_position=&#8221;top_left&#8221; background_repeat=&#8221;repeat&#8221; custom_padding=&#8221;3px|||||&#8221; hover_enabled=&#8221;0&#8243;]<\/p>\n<p>Hey Everyone,<\/p>\n<p>It\u2019s been a hot minute since we aired a new episode of our regular $25\/$50, so it is our pleasure to present exactly that tonight at 10pmET on CBS Sports Network!<\/p>\n<div data-empty=\"true\">\u00a0<\/div>\n<div><a href=\"https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=LbT9hvB-92g&amp;list=PL80pLWeFxFeO9ytdM6NOB3Fx5kvl19vP8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferer noreferrer\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/gallery.eocampaign1.com\/74d178ac-fc7f-11e7-a98f-06b2d989fe84%2F1581715903680-1.png\" width=\"600\" height=\"292.766\" \/><\/a><\/div>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Last week we wrapped up King of the Hill III. If you happened to miss that, fear not, episodes 1-5 are available now, and the finale will be posted on Youtube next Monday.\u00a0<\/p>\n<div data-empty=\"true\">\u00a0<\/div>\n<div><a href=\"https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=KiweVd7JdwE&amp;feature=youtu.be\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferer noreferrer\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/gallery.eocampaign1.com\/74d178ac-fc7f-11e7-a98f-06b2d989fe84%2F1581715974417-2020-02-14+15_22_31-FD+Newsletter+for+2_17_2019+PNIA+-+Google+Docs.png\" width=\"600\" height=\"337.609\" \/><\/a><\/div>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=KiweVd7JdwE&amp;feature=youtu.be\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferer noreferrer\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/gallery.eomail1.com\/74d178ac-fc7f-11e7-a98f-06b2d989fe84%2F1576517180654-1576517180399.png\" width=\"300\" height=\"56.5313\" \/><\/a><\/p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">10pmET TONIGHT: KING OF THE HILL III [THE FINALS]<\/p>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=LbT9hvB-92g&amp;list=PL80pLWeFxFeO9ytdM6NOB3Fx5kvl19vP8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferer noreferrer\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/gallery.eomail2.com\/74d178ac-fc7f-11e7-a98f-06b2d989fe84%2F1580415850829-2020-01-30+14_14_37-WSOP+CHAMP+vs.+THE+BRAIN+_+SEASON+6+EPISODE+44+KING+OF+THE+HILL+III+-+YouTube.png\" width=\"600\" height=\"526.344\" \/><\/a><\/p>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Lastly, worlds collided earlier this week on Survivor: Winners at War. A conversation had by\u00a0previous Survivor champions on Poker Night Live back in 2018 played a major role in this week\u2019s episode. Here\u2019s where it all started.\u00a0<\/p>\n<div data-empty=\"true\">\u00a0<\/div>\n<div><a href=\"https:\/\/youtu.be\/kxsTkHDGc2Y\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferer noreferrer\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/gallery.eocampaign1.com\/74d178ac-fc7f-11e7-a98f-06b2d989fe84%2F1581716176533-2020-02-14+15_22_45-FD+Newsletter+for+2_17_2019+PNIA+-+Google+Docs.png\" width=\"600\" height=\"335.953\" \/><\/a><\/div>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/youtu.be\/kxsTkHDGc2Y\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferer noreferrer\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/gallery.eomail1.com\/74d178ac-fc7f-11e7-a98f-06b2d989fe84%2F1576517180654-1576517180399.png\" width=\"300\" height=\"56.5313\" \/><\/a>\u00a0<\/p>\n<div data-empty=\"true\">\u00a0<\/div>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">If you\u2019ve ever imagined what it would be like to be staked for our $25\/$50 game or given a seat to play on Celebrity Home Game, the first step is playing on the Poker Night in America App. Remember to register, and have your friends join up too. No catch, we just love giving away these sweepstakes awards. You\u2019ll never have an easier call to make in your poker life.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Have a great week, and remember to load up on discount Valentine\u2019s Day candy.<\/p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Your belated Valentine,<br \/>Poker Night in America<\/p>\n<p>[\/et_pb_text][\/et_pb_column][\/et_pb_row][\/et_pb_section]<\/p>\n<span class=\"et_bloom_bottom_trigger\"><\/span>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Hey Everyone, It\u2019s been a hot minute since we aired a new episode of our regular $25\/$50, so it is our pleasure to present exactly that tonight at 10pmET on CBS Sports Network! \u00a0 Last week we wrapped up King of the Hill III. If you happened to miss that, fear not, episodes 1-5 are [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":6,"featured_media":4281,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"gallery","meta":{"_et_pb_use_builder":"on","_et_pb_old_content":"<p dir=\"ltr\"><img class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-4115\" src=\"https:\/\/pokernight.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/01\/2019-01-18-15_00_17-Untitled-document-Google-Docs-1.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1025\" height=\"683\" \/><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">On the sad news of Gavin Smith passing, the Poker Night in America crew wanted to express a few thoughts about one of our favorite players to ever join our table. <\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">It only took a few moments after meeting Gavin to learn a few things about him. First, you would learn immediately that he was genuine. He would tell you exactly what was on his mind, without hesitation or qualification. It\u2019s often said that every word spoken before the word \u201cbut\u201d is BS, and Gavin never used \u201cbut\u201d. He just said everything that came after, and left you to deal with it. <\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Which you usually could, because the next thing that became apparent in Gavin\u2019s presence was that he was hilarious. Swarthy, Canadian-accented humor rolled out of him effortlessly, and cut any tension that his candor might create. As creators of poker entertainment content, we can\u2019t overstate how great it was to have someone like Gavin at our table keeping it active and funny.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Between the lines of his jokes was a rapier wit that never seemed to dull, even in the midst of his well-known excesses. His intelligence was considerable, and seemed to be only matched by his restlessness in life. <\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The final thing that needs to be said is that Gavin Smith knew all the names of the members of our production crew. He may have been the only poker player that has been on our show that can claim that. He partied with us, and cracked us up, and he\u2019d ask about our lives from event to event. It seems small, but to us, it was a big deal. For that, for his candor, and his humor, he\u2019ll always have our love and respect. <\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https:\/\/imgur.com\/a\/MCSQbqY\">Here are some of the photos<\/a> we have of Gavin from his appearances on our show. Please feel free to use these in any way you see fit in your remembrances, with no attribution required.<\/span><\/p><p>If you would like to help the Smith family, a GoFundMe account <a href=\"https:\/\/www.gofundme.com\/rip-ol039-gavin-smith\">has been created here.<\/a><\/p><p>\u00a0<\/p><p>\u00a0<\/p>","_et_gb_content_width":"","_exactmetrics_skip_tracking":fa